Imagine you are the computer. 
Start at the top of the script or the main() function, 
however it's arranged. Go step by step remembering the values of variables, 
or writing them down if they are numerous. Follow loops etc., 
tracking the variables as they change. 
(NB if it's only a specific function or section you have difficulty understanding, 
start there.)When you reach a function call don't step into it at first, 
treat it as a black box and try to understand what parameters it takes 
and what it returns. Where a function is hard to understand in this way 
or poorly documented, repeat the process with that function.
This careful step-by-step reading of the program text should bring you to an 
understanding of how it operates. Then you can try running it and 
adding print statements to see if it behaves as you expect.